  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Quranic Texts**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that `risan/quran-json` provides the complete Quran, comprising all 114 Surahs and 6236 verses. The encoding utilizes authentic Uthmani script, including the initial phrases and letter combinations, providing a solid foundation for analysis.\n\n\n**Verifying Quranic Data Structure**\n\nNow I\'m focusing on validating the data structure. I\'m confirming that the JSON file contains the requisite fields for each verse: sura number, ayah number, and the Uthmani text. I\'m also considering whether to structure the data as a single array of all verses or an array divided by surahs, for better versatility. The data format must be consistent and easy to parse, to ensure accurate analysis of the texts.\n\n\n**Considering Data Structure Flexibility**\n\nI\'m now thinking about how users might want to access this data. Beyond the array of verses, I\'ll also generate a structure with surah details to enhance data flexibility. Specifically, I\'ll generate a comprehensive `quran.json` file in an array of verses format. I\'m also planning to create a second, separate data structure providing a view by surah. I aim to ensure both formats are easily accessible to satisfy varying usage scenarios.\n\n\n"
