  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Exploring Feature Set**\n\nI\'m currently focused on identifying the key features that will make this application comprehensive and enjoyable. I\'m starting by analyzing the user prompt to understand their specific requests. I\'m looking at data sources like quran-json and Quran.com to assess the potential for accessing and using open-source data.\n\n\n**Acquiring Quranic Data**\n\nI\'ve successfully retrieved the complete Uthmani text from the risan/quran-json repository, confirming all 6,236 verses in the correct format. Furthermore, I have generated and stored several JSON files including a comprehensive `quran.json`, a surah-grouped version, and indexes for surahs. This data is available in `assets/data/` within both the public and source directories.\n\n\n**Defining Core Features**\n\nI am now solidifying the essential components of the Quran explorer application. I\'ve broken down the design into Surah Indexing, with browser and search functionality. Then, verse-by-verse and continuous Mushaf reading modes. I\'m also planning to implement global verse search capabilities, and the integration of high-quality audio recitation from EveryAyah.\n\n\n"
