    summary: "The KFGQPC Uthman Taha Naskh font, based on the calligraphy of Uthman Taha and made available by the King Fahd Glorious Quran Printing Complex (KFGQPC), is widely available in TrueType Font (TTF) format. This font is a popular choice for Arabic text in designs and presentations due to its elegant style[1][2].\n\nYou can find the font through several sources:\n*   **Direct Downloads:** Many font websites offer the \"KFGQPC Uthman Taha Naskh Regular\" as a free TrueType Font download[1][3][4][5].\n*   **GitHub Repositories:** A GitHub repository related to \"quranwbw\" also references fonts from the King Fahd Glorious Quran Printing Complex, and it\'s possible to find font files, including TTF, there[6]. Another GitHub issue mentions an OTF attachment, which could also be converted to TTF[7].\n*   **Internet Archive:** The Internet Archive hosts a \"Uthman Taha Naskh - Regular\" font with a TrueType Font download option[8].\n\nWhen downloading, ensure you check the terms and conditions, though the font is generally offered for free by KFGQPC[1][2][5].\n\nSources:\n[1] [arabicfonts.net](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG6gxoLmIfAgM6mOs20QaDAhHbBsj5BQ_C-itrFuaaLKwlNlsHONxakPXxMWeyIELuAshhNPID7ziaO55MmiXfL8RrxXhHnvMTX-OUu-ocbvmDY1-cIXfZDDUv8RGiVADsI4mP8y-5oqZRyOxv2vsPFgRkkYx9-uee9)\n[2] [fontsinuse.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGam8zJy-VY4CtHggRS9V76FVKFFKHKL1MCKHRoqM35gmG48mesrLYzF7jwz8hJY97_-xDJdLwf3Wms8WbTcEkRMpnaLaMjZ9V-2wlxxzXcGHoqzNZlRZUEAEl2wnL0oHREhM54BDRoaXkBr4WPN9Pp6xqMRh-KKGVR0TY=)\n[3] [fontsgeek.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHLRTPL7Ot-2IVVz8zC09ValESuBw0IxEkD1aGnoEb4XAJ98d5Hsiq5Jh9wNoEqykLa5q-DUslcPfaeGSplc_K4wTiNNck4TpBQJsS2Pr5R2TMTSAiaIM6tD0llUQJkWer4Td_JC35W2eDa6WS2H1TsZE1DGZOy3A==)\n[4] [freefonts.co](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFpIqsaKttwprJMb6tgRNdH42D_Mhxltjl5ciOkhvFbnOamvQvn