    summary: "A search for \"KFGQPC\" and font file extensions like \".ttf\" or \".otf\" on GitHub reveals several results related to Arabic fonts, particularly those used for the Quran.\n\nKey findings include:\n*   **KFGQPC Uthmanic Script HAFS Regular**: This is an OpenType Font (OTF) with 1071 glyphs and 2048 units per EM[1]. It is recognized for its historical and cultural significance, having been adopted for drafting the Qur\'an[2]. It is a highly downloaded Arabic font and is compatible for presentations and designs[2].\n*   **KFGQPC Uthman Taha Naskh Regular**: This is a TrueType Font (TTF) that has been downloaded over 400,000 times and has a high user rating[3]. It is also available for free download on various font websites[4]. This font supports the full Arabic alphabet, including diacritics, harakat, and connected letterforms, and can be used for calligraphy, design templates, and branding[5].\n\nSources:\n[1] [fontsgeek.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEiASuxxggix4nGbRhxBlWsFmqiVT1ZgJpJ3Z6tWmY3AqS6DfDpNRIR7rPXWgkerEr3nlUU2ZlCKil7FJ51hUZ1jcXglt33I6Za2wMhFHb4-wk_pGG5DVNMqrCdkraubZVTKqD35vEelBwY9_TTrnHL9j3yfgrLZFXf)\n[2] [arabicfonts.net](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHuCsBTPbcKJUEdBgfiiu3T0XZ3yq0y9C0TILEjfa74_ACqWysZ5Pf4WRozVpMH7yl901rYW0JVjH6bOYzr8CGiy22Qz4rJT0lye1fuMMGz1ru726j9ZooGTPj1ZZtoiFAOyV0Z0Sk8sFTosTV4NVNjYYPigxMddT8McDo=)\n[3] [arabicfonts.net](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFAMkLjv2a96xise0pQTRQznC7JnMkflONoRGFpn1hBQ7r2n2_sfrt8xpdi7kEFUxufp7Z-WYCt4477iYQD9RnGDmy5XfGgTxlDscyvTrcPSWarO-UTEtJf2wR60cJ4k3Y-SqWSEHDDKUO719TjP3tCCsg-FoPX8gc=)\n[4] [freefonts.co](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGjdsIIwPRCZni84db6E50o4m5vww5bqoOzHXUxZtVkru1dg62DmVS1qSJkNVcNWOzvQyT59YjOcL0cM4VsYBw6AiB8IHNqjlYp9MRSojctCXNDm_VCoser1L5mxDZUX_q_mYtmDkRGslwD5PvE4pyP9DxOqMU=)\n[5] [andalusi.app](https://vertexaisearch.cloud