  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Font Matches**\n\nI\'ve homed in on a critical exact match: `uthman_tn1_ver10` and `taha_naskh`, both of which are intriguing. I see a KFGQPC identifier in both. Further investigation is crucial, but I believe I\'m on the right track towards understanding the relationship between the fonts. I need to focus on how the other variables line up.\n\n\n**Revisiting User Intent**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into the user\'s prompt. It looks like they want to integrate a specific font, KFGQPC Uthman Taha Naskh, which is interesting because of the KFGQPC identifier that I\'ve seen before. The user wants the font in .ttf format, which is very clear. It seems to be a key element for the user\'s application, potentially for rendering the Quranic text. I need to figure out what the user aims to gain by introducing the font.\n\n\n**Clarifying User Goals**\n\nI now understand the user wants to implement font selection within an application, specifically to offer users a choice between several Quranic fonts: KFGQPC Uthman Taha Naskh (TTF), KFGQPC Hafs v18, and Amiri Quran. The application will need to load these fonts locally and allow the user to toggle between them. This is more clear from the explicit request for the fonts and the indication of font family definitions.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_202291"
      name: "run_command"
      arguments_json: "{\"CommandLine\":\"node -e \'\\nimport fs from \\\"node:fs\\\";\\nimport path from \\\"node:path\\\";\\n\\nasync function downloadFonts() {\\n  const fonts = [\\n    {\\n      name: \\\"UthmanTahaNaskh.ttf\\\",\\n      url: \\\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/fawazahmed0/quran-api@1/fonts/uthman-tn1-ver10.ttf\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      name: \\\"UthmanTahaNaskh-Bold.ttf\\\",\\n      url: \\\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/fawazahmed0/quran-api@1/fonts/uthman-tn1-b-ver10.ttf\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      name: \\\"KFGQPC-Hafs-v18.ttf\\\",\\n      url: \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thetruetruth/quran-data-kfgqpc/main/hafs/font/hafs.18.ttf\\\"\\n    }\\n  ];\\n\\n  const targetDirs = [\\n    path.resolve(\\\"assets/fonts\\\"),\\n    path.resolve(\\\"public/assets/fonts\\\"),\\n    path.resolve(\\\"src/assets/fonts\\\")\\n  ];\\n\\n  for (const dir of targetDirs) {\\n    fs.mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true });\\n  }\\n\\n  for (const font of fonts) {\\n    console.log(`Downloading ${font.name} from ${font.url}...`);\\n    const res = await fetch(font.url);\\n    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`Failed to download ${font.name}: ${res.statusText}`);\\n    const buffer = Buffer.from(await res.arrayBuffer());\\n    console.log(`Downloaded ${font.name}: ${buffer.byteLength} bytes.`);\\n\\n    for (const dir of targetDirs) {\\n      fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, font.name), buffer);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  console.log(\\\"All fonts downloaded and saved successfully!\\\");\\n}\\n\\ndownloadFonts().catch(err => {\\n  console.error(err);\\n  process.exit(1);\\n});\\n\'\", \"Cwd\":\".\", \"IsDaemon\":false, \"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":20000, \"toolAction\":\"Downloading KFGQPC fonts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Download KFGQPC fonts\"}"
